<title>USA: Indiana/Ohio direct hogs up $1.00 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Indiana/Ohio direct hogs up $1.00 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SPRINGFIELD 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said barrows and gilts were $1.00 higher. Demand was good on a light to moderate run. Top $56.50 per cwt.</p>
<p>US 1-2  230-260 lbs.  55.00-56.00, few 54.50 &amp; 56.50</p>
<p>US 2-3  230-260 lbs.  50.00-54.50</p>
<p>		210-230 lbs.  45.50-50.00</p>
<p>Sows - firm. Top $48.50.</p>
<p>US 1-3  300-450 lbs. 40.00-42.00</p>
<p>		450-500 lbs. 43.00-44.50</p>
<p>		500-600 lbs. 44.00-47.00 Few over 600 lbs.</p>
<p>47.00-48.50</p>
</text>
